/// Synopsis: the documented limits of the animations, each next to its way out where it has one: a `#pause` between the lines of a `>` box shows the box whole on the first step (its bottom edge lightly veiled) and holds back only what follows it; quotations on consecutive lines show on the first step as plain text in quotation marks, while quotations separated by blank lines are revealed one per step; Touying's `#item-by-item` shows every item on every step; numbered items split by a `#pause` inside a box start again at 1 under the veil, and the numbers written by hand (`1.`, `2.`) keep them.
